IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lga-nouns`
IMPORT `lga-time`
IMPORT `lga-defs`
IMPORT `lga-instruments`
IMPORT `lga-register`
IMPORT `lga-compilations`
IMPORT `lga-authorised`
IMPORT `lga-drafting`
IMPORT `lga-scrutiny`
IMPORT `lga-repeal`
IMPORT `lga-sunset`

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), sections 12 to 54 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084 (not the authorised text).
--
-- SEAT: an officer of a department or agency who makes or lodges a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument.
-- The questions are the ones that officer asks: when the instrument commences, what must be lodged and registered, what Parliament can do to it,
-- when it is repealed, and what the Federal Register of Legislation must contain.
-- Nothing here is new law: each question calls the rule already written in the layer-1 modules imported above, and the answer is theirs.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no answers, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices, each with an @desc worded for the officer.
-- A calendar of sitting days is not a plain input, so the questions about sitting days ask the officer for the position of a day in the House's calendar
-- ("the 3rd sitting day after ...", first sitting day counted as 1) or for a date the officer can read off the calendar, and the module's own count is applied to that.
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes a record of facts, the record is built inside the question from the answers; a field the called rule never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment.
-- The answers are MAYBE: JUST TRUE (yes), JUST FALSE (no), NOTHING (the text does not say).

§ `Legislation Act 2003 (sections 12 to 54): the questions of an officer who makes or lodges an instrument`

§§ `Commencement`

-- s 12(1). The default is the start of the day after registration; the instrument's own commencement provision governs "so far as the instrument provides otherwise".
@export When does my instrument commence (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `the day my instrument is registered` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or will) your instrument be registered?
      `my instrument has its own commencement provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument itself say when it commences?
      `the day my instrument's own provision gives` IS A DATE @desc If it does, on what day does its own provision say it commences? (any date if it does not)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does my instrument commence` IS
    IF `s 12(1)(b): the instrument commences in accordance with its own commencement provision` TRUE `my instrument has its own commencement provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `the day my instrument's own provision gives`
    ELSE `s 12(1)(a): the day an instrument commences when it provides nothing else` `the day my instrument is registered`

@export May my instrument say that it commences before it is registered (s 12(1A))?
GIVEN `my instrument is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my instrument commence before it is registered` IS
    `s 12(1A): the instrument, or a provision of it, may provide that it commences before the instrument is registered` `my instrument is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument`

@export If my instrument commences before it is registered, does it stop applying to this person (s 12(2))?
GIVEN `my instrument or the provision commences before it is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your instrument, or the provision, commence before the day it is registered?
      `the person is the Commonwealth or an authority of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Commonwealth or an authority of the Commonwealth?
      `the person's rights as at the time of registration would be disadvantaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the early commencement affect the person's rights as at the time of registration so as to disadvantage them?
      `liabilities would be imposed for things done or omitted before registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the early commencement impose liabilities on the person for anything done or omitted to be done before registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my instrument stop applying to this person` IS
    `s 12(2): the instrument or provision does not apply in relation to the person to the extent of that result`
        `my instrument or the provision commences before it is registered`
        `the person is the Commonwealth or an authority of the Commonwealth`
        `the person's rights as at the time of registration would be disadvantaged`
        `liabilities would be imposed for things done or omitted before registration`

@export Does section 14 allow my instrument to apply, adopt or incorporate this matter from another source (s 14(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the enabling legislation authorises or requires provision about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the enabling legislation authorise or require provision about this matter by legislative instrument or notifiable instrument?
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a contrary intention appear in the enabling legislation or the instrument?
      `the source` IS A `Where the matter comes from` @desc Where does the matter come from: an Act, a legislative instrument that was or is disallowable, rules of court, or any other instrument or writing?
      `the time` IS A `When the matter is taken` @desc As at what time is the matter taken: when your instrument commences, before it commences, a later particular time, or as in force from time to time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 14 allow my instrument to incorporate the matter` IS
    IF `s 14(2): the instrument may not make provision by applying, adopting or incorporating the matter as in force or existing from time to time` `a contrary intention appears` `the source` `the time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `s 14(1): the instrument may make provision in relation to the matter by applying, adopting or incorporating it` `the enabling legislation authorises or requires provision about the matter` `a contrary intention appears` `the source` `the time`

§§ `Lodging and registering`

@export Must I lodge my legislative instrument for registration (s 15G(1))?
GIVEN `my instrument has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your instrument been made?
      `my instrument is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a legislative instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge my legislative instrument` IS
    `s 15G(1): the rule-maker must lodge the instrument for registration as a legislative instrument as soon as practicable after it is made` `my instrument has been made` `my instrument is a legislative instrument`

@export Must I lodge my notifiable instrument for registration (s 15G(2))?
GIVEN `my instrument has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your instrument been made?
      `my instrument is a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a notifiable instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge my notifiable instrument` IS
    `s 15G(2): the rule-maker must lodge the instrument for registration as a notifiable instrument as soon as practicable after it is made` `my instrument has been made` `my instrument is a notifiable instrument`

@export Must I lodge an explanatory statement for my instrument (s 15G(4))?
GIVEN `my instrument is lodged for registration as a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument lodged for registration as a legislative instrument?
      `the statement` IS AN `Explanatory statement` @desc Which statement: the initial one, a supplementary one or a replacement one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge an explanatory statement` IS
    `s 15G(4): the rule-maker must lodge the explanatory statement for registration as soon as practicable` `my instrument is lodged for registration as a legislative instrument` `the statement`

@export Does my initial or replacement explanatory statement meet the requirements (s 15J(2))?
GIVEN `it is approved by me as the rule-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the rule-maker approved the statement?
      `it explains the purpose and operation of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it explain the purpose and operation of the instrument?
      `documents are incorporated by reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any documents incorporated in the instrument by reference?
      `it describes those documents and how to obtain them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it describe the incorporated documents and say how they may be obtained? (yes if there are none)
      `consultation was undertaken under section 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was consultation undertaken under section 17 before the instrument was made?
      `it describes the nature of the consultation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it describe the nature of that consultation? (yes if none was undertaken)
      `it explains why there was no consultation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it explain why no consultation was undertaken? (yes if consultation was undertaken)
      `my instrument is disallowable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a disallowable legislative instrument?
      `it contains a statement of compatibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a statement of compatibility under subsection 9(1) of the Human Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011? (yes if the instrument is not disallowable)
      `it contains the other information prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the other information the regulations prescribe? (yes if they prescribe none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my explanatory statement meet the requirements` IS
    `s 15J(2): the statement meets the requirements for an initial or replacement explanatory statement` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Facts about an initial or replacement explanatory statement` WITH
            `it is approved by the rule-maker` IS `it is approved by me as the rule-maker`
            `it explains the purpose and operation of the instrument` IS `it explains the purpose and operation of the instrument`
            `documents are incorporated in the instrument by reference` IS `documents are incorporated by reference`
            `it contains a description of the incorporated documents and indicates how they may be obtained` IS `it describes those documents and how to obtain them`
            `consultation was undertaken under section 17 before the instrument was made` IS `consultation was undertaken under section 17`
            `it contains a description of the nature of that consultation` IS `it describes the nature of the consultation`
            `it explains why no such consultation was undertaken` IS `it explains why there was no consultation`
            `the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument` IS `my instrument is disallowable`
            `it contains a statement of compatibility prepared under subsection 9(1) of the Human Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011` IS `it contains a statement of compatibility`
            `it contains such other information as is prescribed by regulation` IS `it contains the other information prescribed by regulation`

@export Does my supplementary explanatory statement meet the requirements (s 15J(3))?
GIVEN `it is approved by me as the rule-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the rule-maker approved the statement?
      `it contains the other information prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the other information the regulations prescribe? (yes if they prescribe none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my supplementary explanatory statement meet the requirements` IS
    `s 15J(3): the statement meets the requirements for a supplementary explanatory statement` `it is approved by me as the rule-maker` `it contains the other information prescribed by regulation`

@export Will the First Parliamentary Counsel register what I lodged (s 15H(1))?
GIVEN `I lodged it in accordance with section 15G and the rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lodge it in accordance with section 15G and the rules?
      `how I lodged it` IS A `How lodged` @desc How did you lodge it: as a legislative instrument, as a notifiable instrument, or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the First Parliamentary Counsel register what I lodged` IS
    `s 15H(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel must register the instrument as lodged` `I lodged it in accordance with section 15G and the rules` `how I lodged it`

@export Must the First Parliamentary Counsel refuse to register what I lodged (s 15H(3))?
GIVEN `how I lodged it` IS A `How lodged` @desc How did you lodge it: as a legislative instrument, as a notifiable instrument, or otherwise?
      `the Counsel considers the document not likely to be useful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a document lodged otherwise than as an instrument: does the Counsel consider it not likely to be useful to users of the Register?
      `the Counsel considers registering it inappropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For such a document: does the Counsel consider it would otherwise be inappropriate to register it?
      `I withdrew the lodgement before it was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or someone acting for the responsible person) withdraw the lodgement before it was registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Counsel refuse to register` IS
    `s 15H(3): the First Parliamentary Counsel must not register the instrument or document` `how I lodged it` `the Counsel considers the document not likely to be useful` `the Counsel considers registering it inappropriate` `I withdrew the lodgement before it was registered`

@export Can my legislative instrument be enforced if it is not registered (s 15K(1))?
GIVEN `my instrument is registered as a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument registered as a legislative instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my legislative instrument be enforced` IS
    `s 15K(1): the legislative instrument is enforceable by or against any person (including the Commonwealth)` `my instrument is registered as a legislative instrument`

@export Does my failure to lodge an explanatory statement affect the validity or enforceability of my instrument (s 15K(2))?
GIVEN `I failed to lodge an explanatory statement as section 15G(4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to lodge an explanatory statement as section 15G(4) requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my failure to lodge an explanatory statement affect my instrument` IS
    `s 15K(2): the failure to lodge an explanatory statement affects the validity or enforceability of the instrument` `I failed to lodge an explanatory statement as section 15G(4) requires`

@export Must I tell the First Parliamentary Counsel about this event (s 15L)?
GIVEN `my Act or instrument is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Act or instrument registered?
      `the event` IS AN `Event affecting the Register` @desc Which event has happened?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Counsel about the event` IS
    `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` `my Act or instrument is registered` `the event`

@export Must the Counsel arrange for the correct version of my instrument to be laid before each House (s 15DA(2))?
GIVEN `the Counsel corrected an error in the text of my instrument as it appears in the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the First Parliamentary Counsel rectify an error in the text of your instrument as it appears in the Register?
      `the correction replaced the version that was tabled with another version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the correction replace the version of your disallowable instrument that was tabled with a different version?
      `the tabled version had been laid before a House` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the tabled version already been laid before one or both Houses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Counsel arrange for the correct version to be laid` IS
    `s 15DA(2): the First Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for the correct version to be delivered to each House to be laid` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Facts for section 15DA` WITH
            `the First Parliamentary Counsel rectifies an error referred to in subparagraph 15D(1)(b)(ii)` IS `the Counsel corrected an error in the text of my instrument as it appears in the Register`
            `the rectification results in the originally tabled version of a disallowable legislative instrument being replaced by the correct version` IS `the correction replaced the version that was tabled with another version`
            `at the time of the rectification the originally tabled version has been laid before either or both Houses under subsection 38(1)` IS `the tabled version had been laid before a House`
            -- Placeholder: subsection (2) reads only the first three fields.
            `the instrument has been disallowed at the time it is delivered to a House under subsection (2)` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: subsection (2) reads only the first three fields.
            `the disallowance period for the originally tabled version has ended` IS FALSE

@export Does the Counsel's correction change the time my instrument was registered (s 15D(4))?
GIVEN `it is the correction of an error in the Register in relation to my instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the correction of an error in the Register in relation to your instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a correction change the time of registration` IS
    `s 15D(4): the rectification affects the time at which the instrument is taken to have been registered` `it is the correction of an error in the Register in relation to my instrument`

§§ `Compilations of my instrument`

@export Must I prepare and lodge a compilation of my instrument (s 15R(1))?
GIVEN `a required compilation event has occurred for my instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a required compilation event (such as an express amendment) occurred for your instrument?
      `the rules say section 15R does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the rules prescribe that this duty does not apply to your instrument or in these circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge a compilation` IS
    `s 15R(1): the rule-maker must prepare and lodge a compilation of the instrument for registration` `a required compilation event has occurred for my instrument` `the rules say section 15R does not apply`

@export By when must I lodge the compilation (s 15R(3))?
GIVEN `the day the required compilation event occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the required compilation event occur?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I lodge the compilation` IS
    `s 15R(3): the last day for lodging a compilation after a required compilation event` `the day the required compilation event occurred`

@export Did I lodge the compilation in time (s 15R(3))?
GIVEN `the day the required compilation event occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the required compilation event occur?
      `the day I lodged the compilation` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge the compilation?
      `the Counsel allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the First Parliamentary Counsel allow a longer period?
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that longer period? (any date if there is none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I lodge the compilation in time` IS
    `s 15R(3): the compilation is lodged in time` `the day the required compilation event occurred` `the day I lodged the compilation` `the Counsel allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period`

@export Can the First Parliamentary Counsel require me to lodge a compilation (s 15S(1))?
GIVEN `a discretionary compilation event has occurred for my instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a discretionary compilation event (such as a provision commencing) occurred for your instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Counsel require me to lodge a compilation` IS
    `s 15S(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel may by written notice require the rule-maker to prepare and lodge a compilation within the period stated` `a discretionary compilation event has occurred for my instrument`

@export Does my compilation include everything it must (s 15P)?
GIVEN `it includes the compilation date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the compilation date?
      `editorial changes were made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were any editorial changes made in preparing it?
      `it states that editorial changes were made and outlines them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include a statement that editorial changes have been made and a brief outline of them? (yes if none were made)
      `it includes details of the laws that amend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include details (with commencement details) of any Act or instrument that amends it?
      `it includes the amendment history` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the amendment history of its provisions?
      `it includes the further information the rules prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include any further information the rules prescribe? (yes if they prescribe none)
      `the Counsel is satisfied the amending laws are available on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the First Parliamentary Counsel satisfied the details of amending laws are otherwise available on an approved website?
      `the Counsel is satisfied the amendment history is available on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Counsel satisfied the amendment history is otherwise available on an approved website?
      `the Counsel is satisfied the further information is available on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Counsel satisfied the further prescribed information is otherwise available on an approved website?
      `it says in general terms how to reach that information on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the compilation say in general terms how users can reach that information on the approved website?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my compilation include everything it must` IS
    `s 15P: the registered compilation includes the information it must include` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Facts about a registered compilation` WITH
            `it includes the compilation date` IS `it includes the compilation date`
            `editorial changes were made in preparing it` IS `editorial changes were made`
            `it includes a statement that editorial changes have been made and a brief outline of the changes` IS `it states that editorial changes were made and outlines them`
            `it includes details (including commencement details) of any Act or instrument that amends the principal law` IS `it includes details of the laws that amend it`
            `it includes the amendment history of provisions of the principal law` IS `it includes the amendment history`
            `it includes any further information prescribed by the rules` IS `it includes the further information the rules prescribe`
            `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the details of amending laws are otherwise appropriately available on an approved website` IS `the Counsel is satisfied the amending laws are available on the website`
            `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the amendment history is otherwise appropriately available on an approved website` IS `the Counsel is satisfied the amendment history is available on the website`
            `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the further prescribed information is otherwise appropriately available on an approved website` IS `the Counsel is satisfied the further information is available on the website`
            `the compilation indicates in general terms how users of the Register may access that information on the approved website` IS `it says in general terms how to reach that information on the website`

§§ `Parliamentary scrutiny of my legislative instrument`

@export Must the Office of Parliamentary Counsel arrange for my instrument to be laid before each House (s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my instrument is a registered legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a registered legislative instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my instrument be laid before each House` IS
    `s 38(1): the Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy to be delivered to each House to be laid within 6 sitting days of that House after registration` `my instrument is a registered legislative instrument`

@export Was my instrument laid within the time allowed (s 38(1))?
GIVEN `the sitting day count on which it was laid` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first sitting day of the House after registration as 1, on which sitting day was it laid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my instrument laid in time` IS
    `s 38(1): a sitting day count is within the time for laying` `the sitting day count on which it was laid`

@export Is my instrument repealed because it was not laid in time (s 38(3))?
GIVEN `a copy was not laid before each House in accordance with section 38` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of your instrument not laid before each House in accordance with section 38?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my instrument repealed for not being laid` IS
    `s 38(3): the legislative instrument is repealed` `a copy was not laid before each House in accordance with section 38`

@export From what day is my instrument no longer in force for not being laid (s 38(3))?
GIVEN `the last day for laying it before the House of Representatives` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which it could be laid before the House of Representatives?
      `the last day for laying it before the Senate` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which it could be laid before the Senate?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day is my instrument no longer in force` IS
    `s 38(3): the first day on which the legislative instrument is no longer in force for not being laid` `the last day for laying it before the House of Representatives` `the last day for laying it before the Senate`

-- The last input of the called rule is section 51(4), the case of a certificate under section 51; it is passed as FALSE because this question is about the officer's own instrument.
@export Is my instrument subject to disallowance (s 4, ss 42 and 44)?
GIVEN `the enabling legislation facilitates an intergovernmental body or scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the enabling legislation (not the Corporations Act 2001) facilitate the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and a State or Territory?
      `the enabling legislation authorises the body or scheme to make the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it authorise the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme?
      `my instrument is a regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a regulation?
      `an Act makes it disallowable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the enabling legislation or another Act have the effect that the instrument is disallowable?
      `an Act says section 42 does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act declare, or have the effect, that section 42 does not apply to the instrument?
      `a regulation prescribes it as not disallowable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument prescribed by regulation as one to which section 42 does not apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my instrument subject to disallowance` IS
    `s 4: the legislative instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument`
        (`s 44(1): section 42 does not apply in relation to the instrument` `the enabling legislation facilitates an intergovernmental body or scheme` `the enabling legislation authorises the body or scheme to make the instrument` `my instrument is a regulation` `an Act makes it disallowable` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        (`s 44(2): section 42 does not apply in relation to the instrument or provision` `an Act says section 42 does not apply` `a regulation prescribes it as not disallowable` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        FALSE

@export Is a notice of a motion to disallow my instrument still in time (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `the sitting day count on which notice is given` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first sitting day of that House after your instrument was laid before it as 1, on which sitting day was (or would be) the notice given?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a notice of motion to disallow in time` IS
    `s 42(1): a sitting day count is within the time allowed` `the sitting day count on which notice is given`

@export Is my instrument disallowed (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `notice of a motion to disallow was given within 15 sitting days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of a motion to disallow given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House after your instrument was laid before it?
      `the House passed the resolution within 15 sitting days of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that House pass a resolution disallowing it within 15 sitting days after the notice was given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my instrument disallowed` IS
    `s 42(1): the instrument or provision so disallowed is repealed immediately after the passing of that resolution` `notice of a motion to disallow was given within 15 sitting days` `the House passed the resolution within 15 sitting days of the notice`

@export If my instrument is disallowed, does the law it repealed come back (s 45)?
GIVEN `my instrument was repealed by section 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your instrument repealed by section 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)?
      `it had repealed another instrument or law that was in force before it commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your instrument wholly or partly repealed another instrument or law that was in force immediately before it commenced?
      `sunsetting would have repealed that other law first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Part 4 (sunsetting) have repealed that other instrument or law before the date it would be revived?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the repealed law revive` IS
    `s 45: the instrument, law or provision repealed by the repealing instrument or provision revives from the repeal time` `my instrument was repealed by section 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` `it had repealed another instrument or law that was in force before it commenced` `sunsetting would have repealed that other law first`

@export Am I barred from making a new instrument the same in substance as one already registered (s 46)?
GIVEN `the original instrument has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the original instrument been registered?
      `the new instrument is the same in substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new instrument the same in substance as the original?
      `the day the original was registered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the original registered?
      `the day it was laid before both Houses` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it laid before both Houses (the later day, if they differ) -- or, if it has not been laid before both, the last day on which it could have been laid?
      `the day I would make the new instrument` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you make the new instrument?
      `both Houses approve by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have both Houses approved by resolution the making of an instrument the same in substance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from making the same instrument again under section 46` IS
    `s 46(1): the same legislative instrument is not to be made during the period`
        `the original instrument has been registered`
        `the new instrument is the same in substance`
        (`s 46(2): a day falls in the period starting on the day of registration and ending at the end of its last day` `the day the original was registered` (`s 46(2): the last day of the period in which the same instrument is not to be made` `the day it was laid before both Houses`) `the day I would make the new instrument`)
        `both Houses approve by resolution`

@export Am I barred from making a new instrument the same in substance while a notice of disallowance is pending (s 47(1))?
GIVEN `notice of a motion to disallow was given in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of a motion to disallow the instrument given within 15 sitting days after it was laid?
      `the notice has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice been withdrawn?
      `it is taken to have been disallowed under section 42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument taken to have been disallowed under subsection 42(2)?
      `the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the motion been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of?
      `section 42(3) has applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has subsection 42(3) (dissolution, expiry or prorogation) applied to the instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the same instrument barred while a notice is pending` IS
    `s 47(1): the same legislative instrument or provision must not be made` `notice of a motion to disallow was given in time` `the notice has been withdrawn` `it is taken to have been disallowed under section 42(2)` `the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` `section 42(3) has applied`

@export Am I barred from making a new instrument the same in substance as one that was disallowed (s 48(1))?
GIVEN `it is the same in substance as one disallowed under section 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new instrument the same in substance as one that was disallowed (or taken to have been disallowed) under subsection 42(1) or (2)?
      `the day of disallowance` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the instrument disallowed?
      `the day I would make the new instrument` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you make the new instrument?
      `the relevant House approved by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the House in which notice of the motion to disallow was given approved by resolution the making of the new instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the same instrument barred after disallowance` IS
    `s 48(1): the later legislative instrument or provision must not be made on that day` `it is the same in substance as one disallowed under section 42` `the day of disallowance` `the day I would make the new instrument` `the relevant House approved by resolution`

§§ `Automatic repeal of my instrument or its provisions`

@export Will my amending or repealing instrument be repealed automatically (s 48A(1))?
GIVEN `my instrument is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument?
      `its only legal effect is to amend or repeal other instruments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its only legal effect to amend or repeal one or more other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments?
      `it makes an application, saving or transitional provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it make any application, saving or transitional provision relating to the amendment or repeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my amending instrument repealed automatically` IS
    `s 48A(1): this section repeals the instrument` `my instrument is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` `its only legal effect is to amend or repeal other instruments` `it makes an application, saving or transitional provision`

@export On what day will my amending or repealing instrument be repealed automatically (s 48A(2))?
GIVEN `my instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument a disallowable legislative instrument?
      `the last day on which it may be disallowed in a House` IS A DATE @desc If it is disallowable, what is the last day on which it may be disallowed in a House? (any date if it is not)
      `the day it commenced, or its last provision commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day did it commence (or, if it has several commencements, its last provision)?
      `the day it was registered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my amending instrument repealed` IS
    `s 48A(2): the day on which the repeal by this section happens` `my instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument` `the last day on which it may be disallowed in a House` `the day it commenced, or its last provision commenced` `the day it was registered`

@export Will this provision of my instrument be repealed automatically as an amending or repealing provision (s 48C(1))?
GIVEN `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a provision of a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument?
      `the instrument is one described in section 48A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument one whose only legal effect is to amend or repeal other instruments (so that section 48A applies to it)?
      `its only effect is to amend or repeal other instruments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only legal effect of the provision (alone or with others) to amend or repeal other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments?
      `its only effect is to amend its own instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only legal effect of the provision (alone or with others) to amend the instrument that contains it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my provision repealed automatically as an amending provision` IS
    `s 48C(1): this section repeals the provision` `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` `the instrument is one described in section 48A(1)` `its only effect is to amend or repeal other instruments` `its only effect is to amend its own instrument`

@export Will this commencement provision of my instrument be repealed automatically (s 48D(1))?
GIVEN `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument that is not a commencement instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a provision of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, other than a commencement instrument?
      `it provides solely for commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide solely for the commencement of the instrument, an Act or another instrument, or a provision of one of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my commencement provision repealed automatically` IS
    `s 48D(1): this section repeals the commencement provision` `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument that is not a commencement instrument` `it provides solely for commencement`

§§ `Sunsetting of my legislative instrument`

@export On what day will my legislative instrument be repealed by sunsetting (s 50)?
GIVEN `the day my instrument was registered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your instrument registered?
      `the year my instrument was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it made? (needed only if it was registered on 1 January 2005)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my instrument sunset` IS
    `ss 50(1) and (2): the day a legislative instrument is repealed by sunsetting, by registration day and year made` `the day my instrument was registered` `the year my instrument was made`

@export Is my instrument exempt from sunsetting (s 54)?
GIVEN `the enabling legislation facilitates an intergovernmental body or scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the enabling legislation (not the Corporations Act 2001) facilitate the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and a State or Territory?
      `the enabling legislation authorises the body or scheme to make the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it authorise the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme?
      `an Act says Part 4 does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act provide, or have the effect, that Part 4 does not apply to the instrument?
      `a regulation prescribes it as exempt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 54(2)(b)?
      `it is a regulation made for one of the listed purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a regulation made for the purposes of paragraph 8(6)(b), 10(1)(c), 11(2)(b), 44(2)(b) or 54(2)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my instrument exempt from sunsetting` IS
    IF `s 54(1): this Part does not apply in relation to the legislative instrument` `the enabling legislation facilitates an intergovernmental body or scheme` `the enabling legislation authorises the body or scheme to make the instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `s 54(2): this Part does not apply in relation to the legislative instrument` `an Act says Part 4 does not apply` `a regulation prescribes it as exempt` `it is a regulation made for one of the listed purposes`

@export May the Attorney-General defer the sunsetting of my instrument by certificate (s 51(1))?
GIVEN `it would be repealed by section 50 or 51A on its sunsetting day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your instrument, apart from section 51, be repealed by section 50 or 51A on its sunsetting day?
      `likely to cease to be in force within 24 months after that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Attorney-General satisfied, on your written application, that it would otherwise be likely to cease to be in force within 24 months after that day?
      `a substitute cannot be completed in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Attorney-General satisfied, on your written application, that a substitute instrument cannot be completed before that day for reasons you could not have foreseen and avoided?
      `the Attorney-General has approved this Part not applying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Attorney-General satisfied, on your written application, that the Attorney-General has approved this Part not applying to the instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Attorney-General defer the sunsetting` IS
    `s 51(1)(c): the Attorney-General may issue a certificate providing that the instrument is repealed by section 51 on a 1 April or 1 October that is on or before the second anniversary of the sunsetting day` `it would be repealed by section 50 or 51A on its sunsetting day` `likely to cease to be in force within 24 months after that day` `a substitute cannot be completed in time` `the Attorney-General has approved this Part not applying`

@export Is the day I want in a deferral certificate one the section allows (s 51(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the sunsetting day` IS A DATE @desc What is the instrument's sunsetting day?
      `the day I want the certificate to specify` IS A DATE @desc What day do you want the certificate to specify?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day in my certificate allowed` IS
    `s 51(1)(c): the day specified is a 1 April or 1 October on or before the second anniversary of the sunsetting day` `the sunsetting day` `the day I want the certificate to specify`

@export Will a resolution of a House keep my instrument in force (s 53(1))?
GIVEN `my instrument would otherwise be repealed on the repeal day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your instrument otherwise be repealed on its repeal day by section 50, 51 or 51A?
      `it is mentioned in a certificate copy or a list laid before a House` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it mentioned in a copy of a section 51 certificate laid before a House, or in a list laid under section 52?
      `the House passed a resolution that it should continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that House pass a resolution indicating that it should continue in force?
      `the day the House passed the resolution` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the House pass the resolution?
      `the repeal day` IS A DATE @desc What is the repeal day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will a resolution keep my instrument in force` IS
    `s 53(1): the legislative instrument continues in force despite sections 50, 51 and 51A` `my instrument would otherwise be repealed on the repeal day` `it is mentioned in a certificate copy or a list laid before a House` `the House passed a resolution that it should continue` `the day the House passed the resolution` `the repeal day`

@export Will I be sent a copy of the list of instruments due for sunsetting (s 52(3))?
GIVEN `a list has been laid before either House` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a list under section 52(2) been laid before either House?
      `my instrument is on the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your instrument on the list?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be sent a copy of the list` IS
    `s 52(3): the Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of the list to be provided to the rule-maker responsible for the legislative instrument` `a list has been laid before either House` `my instrument is on the list`

§§ `What the Federal Register of Legislation must contain`

@export Must the Register contain this document (s 15A(2))?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which kind of document is it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Register contain the document` IS
    `s 15A(2): the Register must contain the document` `the document`

@export May the Register contain this additional document (s 15A(3))?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which kind of document is it?
      `the Counsel considers it likely to be useful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the First Parliamentary Counsel consider the document likely to be useful to users of the Register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Register contain the additional document` IS
    `s 15A(3): the Register may contain the additional document` `the document` `the Counsel considers it likely to be useful`

@export Must the Counsel record a correction in the Register (s 15D(2))?
GIVEN `a correction has been made to the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the First Parliamentary Counsel corrected an error in the Register under section 15D(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Counsel record the correction` IS
    `s 15D(2): the First Parliamentary Counsel must include a statement of the rectification and a brief outline in the Register` `a correction has been made to the Register`

@export Is this copy an authorised version of my instrument (s 15ZA)?
GIVEN `it is an electronic copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an electronic copy?
      `it is a printed copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a printed copy?
      `it is from an approved website in the prescribed format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website in a format the rules prescribe?
      `the website says it is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the website indicate, in the way the rules prescribe, that such a copy is an authorised version?
      `the copy says it is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy itself indicate, in the way the rules prescribe, that it is an authorised version?
      `it is in the prescribed format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in a format the rules prescribe?
      `it was printed directly from an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a printed copy, was it produced directly from another version that is an authorised version?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this copy an authorised version` IS
    `s 15ZA: the copy of the registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version` `it is an electronic copy` `it is a printed copy` `it is from an approved website in the prescribed format` `the website says it is an authorised version` `the copy says it is an authorised version` `it is in the prescribed format` `it was printed directly from an authorised version`

@export Is proof not required in court of a matter about my instrument that section 15ZB lists (s 15ZB(1))?
GIVEN `the matter arises in proceedings in a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter arise in proceedings in a court or tribunal?
      `the matter` IS A `Matter for section 15ZB(1)` @desc Which matter: the assent, the making, the text, the registration, the commencement, editorial changes, a compilation's text and date, or whether a copy is authorised?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is proof of the matter not required in court` IS
    `s 15ZB(1): proof is not required about the matter` `the matter arises in proceedings in a court or tribunal` `the matter`
